     "body": "Red on Windows at untouched origin/main 191f3c0af (xiaomi-gpu, Windows 11, Go 1.26.8, `win-run go test -count=1 ./internal/agent/`):\n\n```\n--- FAIL: TestCodexOwnModelsFollowPicks (0.18s)\n    codex_own_test.go:53: a look at Codex's ticks made 74 allocations, want at most 20\n```\n\nSearched by name: not in #4786, #4115, #1827, #1388, #2808. It is an allocation bar like #4786's six, and 74 is in the range those read there (67 to 82), so likely the same cause: `provider.StampNow`'s `environSum` makes a string per environment variable on Windows each call. Not traced further; the other 24 agent reds in the same run are already filed (#4115, #4786, #4785, #5068, #5069, #5070, #5130, #5343, #5344, #1827, #1388, #2808, #4033, #2775, #5019).\n",
